# No vendor or agent attribution in git

Git history, branches, tags, and pull requests must read as ordinary human work. Do not name Cursor, Codex, Claude, Copilot, ChatGPT, Grok, or any other agent, model, or tool.

Never add:

- `Co-authored-by`, `Signed-off-by`, `Made-with`, `Generated-by`, or similar trailers for an agent
- Session links, agent IDs, or "made with" badges
- Tool or model names in commit subjects or bodies
- Agent names in branch names, tags, PR titles, or PR bodies

If a hook, UI, or wrapper appends a trailer, strip it before the commit is created. Rewrite the message if one already landed and the commit has not been pushed.

```
# BAD
Add tee and stroke-index setup

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>

# BAD
feat: handicap screen [claude]

# GOOD
Add tee and stroke-index setup
```
